- `Txn.close_remainder_to()` - could allow an attacker to close the account and send remaining funds
- `Txn.asset_close_to()` - not applicable here but shows general pattern

Since this is a smart signature (stateless contract) that authorizes application calls, the absence of these checks is particularly dangerous. An attacker could craft a transaction group where the first transaction (application call) has malicious rekey_to or close_remainder_to fields while still passing all the other checks.

